error[E0262]: a '..=' statement appends to a string, but the destination is int32
 --> $DIR/concatenation-integer.nra:6:7
  |
6 |     n ..= 5;
  |       ^^^ '..=' as a statement
  |     - this has type int32
  |
  = note: as a statement, 'place ..= text;' appends text to a string; in an expression, 'start ..= stop' is an inclusive range
  = help: to make an inclusive range, use it as a value: 'let r = start ..= stop;'

For more information about this error, try `neura explain E0262`.
